# Product features and pricing

This repository studies how product features relate to prices across categories.
Chocolate sold in the UK is the current example. Preserve original information
and evidence before deriving an analytical schema or fitting a pricing model.

| Document | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| [Intention](docs/intention.md) | Goals, delivery order and constraints. |
| [Specification](docs/spec.md) | Contracts, pricing methodology and acceptance requirements. |
| [Chocolate silver](docs/chocolate-silver.md) | Raw/silver workflow, outputs, evidence resolution and reproducibility. |
| [Chocolate schema](docs/chocolate-schema.md) | Typed fields, evidence reviews and model handoff. |
| [Portable processing](docs/category-processing.md) | Profiles, mapping maintenance and model preparation. |
| [Compatibility guides](docs/chocolate-deduplication.md), [cleanup](docs/chocolate-cleaning.md) | Standalone diagnostic helpers and their distinct contracts. |
| [Chocolate pricing design](docs/chocolate-modeling-design.md), [LightGBM/SHAP explanations](docs/analysis/lightgbm-shap-explanation-design.md) | Proposed models, comparisons, calibration and explanations. |
| [Chocolate contract manifest](schemas/chocolate/dataset-contract.json), [dataset contract guide](docs/dataset-contracts.md) | Pinned schema, mappings, validator and model design; storage, caches and offline use. |
| [Collection package](plugins/category-research/README.md), [processing package](plugins/category-processing/README.md) | Agent Plugins 1.0.0 packages, skills, CLI and Python API. |
